-- BetterUI duel readout (match HUD; docs/game/ui/duel-readout.md). After a focus duel decided by a special move against
-- a special move, or by a power charge / power block against a special move, each player's total (the values the
-- game compared: BetterUI's scripts\duel_readout.lua reads them from the resolver, CMND_BETTERUI_DUEL_READOUT) is shown
-- on the shot readout's plates: left the player's side, right the rival's, each «<label> <total>». Plates: layers
-- clean_hud_duel_telop_self / _enemy (the retail objects of the shot readout, BetterUI content\menus\duel_readout.toml),
-- opened, filled and animated as the retail shot readout does (soccer_shoot_catch_info_menu); their picture label and
-- their brecha / save block hidden. Labels: layer clean_hud_duel_label (2 instances, a text node), kept every frame on
-- each plate's label slot through the meshes' global positions (the offset between the label layer's position and its
-- text node's global position is measured once per HUD, so no anchor or screen origin is assumed).
-- Switch: Mods options «Duel counter» (clean_hud.duel_readout, read once per duel: no restart). Plain line duels never
-- reach the resolver, so they show nothing. Wrappers only (OnInit, OnOpenLayer, Step); no engine call at chunk load.

